One of the few good features of the U.S. defintion of obscenity is
that it requires a work to be considered as a whole. I interpret this
to mean (and I don't know if any judges agree with me) that a newsgroup
cannot be illegal if it has some literary, etc. merit.

In other words, rather than one bad apple spoiling the whole bunch,
one good apple (if it cannot be separated practically from the rest)
saves the whole bunch.

[There is U.S. case law on "separated practically", but I don't
know the details.]

I don't know if Canadian law has a similar concept.

- Carl

